  To finally answer the "identification" part of your subject.  Trying
too hard to identify items too early is a deathtrap.  Monsters will
identify emergency items for you when they use them.  Harmful potions
will be identified when they throw them at you.

  Leave potions, spellbooks, scrolls by the downstairs just before
descending.  This will save them from freezing, burning, blanking,
dilution, etc.  If you have positively identified emergency scrolls or
potions, carry some with you.


  Your main identification goals early are armor and wands, because you
can do so safely.


  Try on all non-cursed armor you find.  (Use your pet to identify it as
non-cursed.)  Lower AC compensates for a number of other deficiencies.
Learn how to identify wands.  (There are spoilers.)  




